1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,760
So, short version.

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:06,320
Two hundred thousand dollars in my trunk,
and a woman named Laura on the phone,

3
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:08,400
begging me not to go to the police.

4
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:12,000
I didn't. I drove to the
diner she picked instead,

5
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:15,280
with the bag riding shotgun and
my eyes glued to the mirror.

6
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:18,560
She was in a back booth,
still in her scrubs,

7
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:19,920
and her coffee looked cold.

8
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:22,080
"I'm Laura," she said.

9
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:24,800
"I'm a nurse. I came
straight from my shift."

10
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:28,560
Her dad, Harold, had done
the books at Brandt Markets,

11
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:30,720
the grocery chain, for twenty years.

12
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:33,960
Earlier that night,
he'd sent her one text.

13
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:36,400
"If anything happens, find the driver.

14
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:38,880
His name is Kai. Here's his number.

15
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:42,760
You can trust him." And
then his phone went dead.

16
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:44,400
"Why would he trust me?"

17
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:47,040
I said. "I'm just the rideshare guy.

18
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:49,360
I can't even make the
payments on my rental.

19
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:50,720
I drove him to the airport.

20
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:53,440
That's it." She just
looked at me and said,

21
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,600
"I was hoping you could tell me."

22
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:58,893
She wanted me to hang on
to the bag until morning,

23
00:00:58,947 --> 00:01:00,707
so her lawyer could take it.

24
00:01:00,813 --> 00:01:02,947
"Just until eight," she said.

25
00:01:02,973 --> 00:01:05,520
"I'll give you five thousand
dollars for your trouble.

26
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:07,080
My own money."

27
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:08,520
Five grand.

28
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:11,360
That would cover the car,
with some left over.

29
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:16,400
I was literally opening my mouth to say
yes when the bell over the door jingled.

30
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:19,600
A guy in a gray jacket and
a baseball cap walked in,

31
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:22,800
totally relaxed, and took
a seat at the counter.

32
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:24,440
Laura went white.

33
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:26,520
"That's him," she whispered.

34
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:28,000
"He works for Brandt.

35
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:30,680
He's been following me
since I left the hospital.

36
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:32,000
I need a minute."

37
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:35,107
She slid out of the booth
and headed for the restroom.

38
00:01:35,133 --> 00:01:37,680
And the guy in the gray
jacket picked up his coffee,

39
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:40,947
strolled over, and sat down
right where she'd been.

40
00:01:40,973 --> 00:01:42,173
"Kai, right?"

41
00:01:42,227 --> 00:01:44,000
he said. "I'm Vince.

42
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:45,720
Let's talk like adults."

43
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:50,280
"Fifty grand," Vince said,
"and the bag leaves with me.

44
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:51,920
Cash, tonight.

45
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,480
Nobody ever knows you were involved."

46
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:57,560
I asked him why I should
believe him over her.

47
00:01:57,600 --> 00:01:59,493
He just turned his phone around.

48
00:01:59,547 --> 00:02:02,507
A theft report, with Harold
Pruitt's name on it.

49
00:02:02,533 --> 00:02:05,573
"Her father stole from my boss," he said.

50
00:02:05,627 --> 00:02:08,440
"She's trying to get the money
back before the police do.

51
00:02:08,480 --> 00:02:10,200
She's lying to you, Kai.

52
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:11,960
You seem like a decent guy.

53
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,640
Don't go down with them."

54
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:16,040
I looked past him, out the window.

55
00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:18,840
Laura was in the parking
lot now, on the phone,

56
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:21,600
crying, one hand over her mouth.

57
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:23,640
Fifty thousand dollars.

58
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:26,760
The hospital, the car,
the rest of the year,

59
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:29,480
all taken care of with one handshake.

60
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:34,480
Or a nurse crying in a parking lot,
and a bag I didn't understand.

61
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:39,400
So, fifty grand in cash, or a
nurse crying in a parking lot.

62
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:42,600
Your call. If you think I
should take the fifty grand,

63
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:44,440
tap the video on the left.

64
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:48,120
If I should run with Laura and the
bag, tap the one on the right.

65
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:50,600
And you can always come back
and try the other path.
